      "brief": "# durable memory\n<match path=\"~/.stella/memories/MEMORY.md\" lines=\"26-34\">\n29: ## 2026-07-18 20:14 — Recall latency root-caused (LLM/seed overhead, not SQLite) + Codex memory architecture reverse-engineered with Stella adoption plan\n30: Threads: root-cause-why-stella-s-recall-memory-search-is:local:sub:fcf2b043-0291-4962-9cf5-aa0e660101bb, reverse-engineer-chatgpt-desktop-app-codex-repo:local:sub:e82d9d8b-6d91-4667-b64b-a9833f7b386a\n31: Why this matters: Recall feels slow (median 28.1s over 49 calls, p90 88.4s) despite millisecond SQLite/FTS retrieval, and Codex's shipped memory design shows how to shrink the payload and skip the LLM for common lookups.\n32: Outcome: Recall analysis (strictly read-only, mode=ro + query_only, no code changed): retrieval is NOT the bottleneck — 2.13GB live DB, both FTS indexes complete/backfilled (Jul 11), representative searches 1–20ms (unused LIKE fallback would be 3.7s). Real causes, ranked: (1) oversized eager seed — every source pre-searched, avg 45,286 chars, p90 53,642; (2) serial model/tool rounds (avg 3.45 extra searches, +17.7K chars median); (3) orchestrator invoked Recall twice in 7 of 10 recent runs (+5–14s between calls); (4) wrong utility route — Recall spawns a fresh one-shot Claude CLI on `claude-code/fable` (saved claudeCodeModel outranks the stella/light pin in claude-code-agent-runtime.ts:62), not the benchmarked `gpt-5.6-luna`; latest 27.5s call did ZERO model-initiated searches; (5) unranked substring memory search; (6) minor N+1s (transcript neighbors, active threads, 800-event load for 5 rows). July 11's 599–4,560s outliers predate the route-resolution fix (historical, not current). Recommended: one parallel retrieval pass + one synthesis call capped ~8–12KB with single reformulation fallback; pin Recall to Luna/off independent of engine; cache same-turn Recall with structured found/no_match status; intent-based source routing; compact structured routing index (MEMORY.md is 1.12MB, summary 30.8KB); batch secondary reads; phase-level timing telemetry. Codex reverse-engineering (ChatGPT.app 26.715.31251 bundling codex-cli 0.145.0-alpha.18, asar extracted read-only; source pulled ff-only to `35eaf3ffb`): memory is SQLite `~/.codex/memories_1.sqlite` stage1_outputs (428 rows, 256 selected, 120 cited) + progressive-disclosure files — `memory_summary.md` always injected capped 2,500 tokens, `MEMORY.md` (469KB) as primary grep target, per-rollout summaries, skills, private git baseline for incremental diffs. Phase 1 = background LLM per idle rollout (gpt-5.6-luna, low reasoning, concurrency 8, strict JSON, relevance gate, secrets redacted). Phase 2 (Dream equivalent, `memory_consolidate_global`) = locked-down consolidation agent (gpt-5.6-terra, medium, no network/agents/MCP, 6h cooldown, skips LLM when git diff is clean). No embeddings/vector DB anywhere — model-directed rg/substring search driven by an explicit injected decision contract; hidden citation blocks bump usage_count/last_usage, closing a retention feedback loop. Stella adoption recs: deterministic no-LLM `search_memory` fast path for the orchestrator; make memory_summary a real routing index; complete the unused usage-feedback loop (`recordUsage()` has no call site); normalize Dream inputs via cheap structured extraction; deterministic incremental diff for Dream; split cheap/strong background models with a 25%-quota guard — while keeping Remember-owned profile.md, pre-compaction flush, and FTS5 episodic search. Only mutation across both tasks: the authorized ff-only pull of ~/workspaces/codex.\n33: Recall hooks: Recall slow root cause 28s median seed 45K chars eager, claude-code fable wrong utility model one-shot CLI spawn, duplicate same-turn Recall calls orchestrator, FTS healthy milliseconds LIKE fallback 3.7s unused, gpt-5.6-luna utility route recommendation cap 8-12KB, Codex memories_1.sqlite stage1_outputs usage_count citations, memory_summary 2500 tokens always injected MEMORY.md grep target, Phase 1 luna Phase 2 terra memory_consolidate_global git baseline six hour cooldown, no embeddings substring rg decision contract, search_memory deterministic fast path routing index, recordUsage no call site feedback loop, normalize Dream inputs structured extraction quota guard\n34: \n</match>"
    },
